.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.TH voltkit 1  "Voltkit 0.2.0" "Voltkit Manual"
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SH NAME
voltkit \- A unified suite of PowerToys\-style micro\-utilities for Linux
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBvoltkit\fR [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] [\fB\-V\fR|\fB\-\-version\fR] [\fIsubcommands\fR]
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SH DESCRIPTION
PowerToys\-style micro\-utilities for Linux, in one binary.
.PP
Run without a subcommand to open the GTK control center. Each subcommand runs one utility from the terminal, a script or a keyboard shortcut.
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
.TP
\fB\-V\fR, \fB\-\-version\fR
Print version
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SH SUBCOMMANDS
.TP
voltkit\-ocr(1)
Select a screen region and copy the recognized text to the clipboard
.TP
voltkit\-pick\-color(1)
Pick a color from the screen and copy its HEX value
.TP
voltkit\-color(1)
Convert a color (#hex or rgb(...)) and report WCAG contrast
.TP
voltkit\-compress(1)
Strip metadata and compress PNG, JPEG, WebP or MP4 files
.TP
voltkit\-expand(1)
Expand a snippet template, e.g. "Sent {date:%A}: {clipboard}"
.TP
voltkit\-picker(1)
Open the snippet picker and paste the chosen snippet into the focused app
.TP
voltkit\-expander(1)
Set up and toggle typed triggers (type ;date anywhere to expand it)
.TP
voltkit\-ruler(1)
Measure distances on screen in pixels
.TP
voltkit\-awake(1)
Keep the computer from sleeping or locking its screen
.TP
voltkit\-qr(1)
Read QR codes from the screen or image files, or make them from text
.TP
voltkit\-daemon(1)
Run the background service that listens for global shortcuts
.TP
voltkit\-doctor(1)
Check that everything Voltkit needs is installed and set up
.TP
voltkit\-trigger(1)
Run a hotkey action via the daemon, or directly if it isn\*(Aqt running
.TP
voltkit\-shortcuts(1)
Manage GNOME keybindings for desktops without the GlobalShortcuts portal
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
Open the control center:
.RS 4
.nf
\fBvoltkit\fR
.fi
.RE
.PP
Copy text from part of the screen:
.RS 4
.nf
\fBvoltkit ocr\fR
.fi
.RE
.PP
Check a color\*(Aqs contrast:
.RS 4
.nf
\fBvoltkit color \*(Aq#3584e4\*(Aq\fR
.fi
.RE
.PP
Start the background service at every login:
.RS 4
.nf
\fBvoltkit daemon enable\-autostart\fR
.fi
.RE
.SH FILES
.TP
\fB~/.config/voltkit/config.toml\fR
Configuration: hotkeys, OCR language, compression quality and snippets. Every key is optional.
.TP
\fB~/.local/share/voltkit/colors.txt\fR
Color history, newest first, shared by pick\-color, the daemon and the control center.
.TP
\fB~/.config/autostart/io.github.arios4k.Voltkit.Daemon.desktop\fR
Created by voltkit daemon enable\-autostart.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
\fBWAYLAND_DISPLAY\fR
When set, the clipboard is accessed with wl\-copy and wl\-paste; otherwise with xclip.
.TP
\fBXDG_CONFIG_HOME, XDG_DATA_HOME\fR
Override the base directories of the files listed above.
.SH "EXIT STATUS"
.PP
0 on success, 1 on any error. Errors are printed to standard error.
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SH "SEE ALSO"
\fBvoltkit\-ocr\fR(1), \fBvoltkit\-pick\-color\fR(1), \fBvoltkit\-color\fR(1), \fBvoltkit\-compress\fR(1), \fBvoltkit\-expand\fR(1), \fBvoltkit\-picker\fR(1), \fBvoltkit\-expander\fR(1), \fBvoltkit\-ruler\fR(1), \fBvoltkit\-awake\fR(1), \fBvoltkit\-qr\fR(1), \fBvoltkit\-daemon\fR(1), \fBvoltkit\-doctor\fR(1), \fBvoltkit\-trigger\fR(1), \fBvoltkit\-shortcuts\fR(1)
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
